bench/attribution.patch: temporary stage timers for bench/attribution.ts. Apply with
`git apply bench/attribution.patch`, rebuild the release addon, run attribution.ts,
then `git checkout -- Cargo.lock crates/ packages/brust/src/worker.ts` and
`rm crates/brust-server/src/perf.rs`. Never commit the applied patch.

Refreshed after M3-P P5 (lane m3p-a-alloc-bridge): call_worker now awaits the
dispatch future inline inside a `Detach` wrapper (no per-call tokio::spawn, no
JoinHandle). Stage changes vs the previous patch:
  - CW_SPAWN_SCHED (63/83) and CW_JOIN (67/87) are no longer recorded: there is no
    spawn to schedule and no join to wait on. The ids stay in perf.rs; attribution.ts
    skips a stage with zero calls.
  - CW_CLAIM, CW_SER, CW_REQ_BYTES, CW_DISPATCH, CW_RESP_BYTES, the worker perf tail
    (CW_RUST_TO_JS .. CW_JS_TO_RUST), CW_READ_PARSE and CW_TOTAL keep their ids and
    meaning; the timers for DISPATCH..READ_PARSE live inside the Detach'd future.
    CW_TOTAL now also covers the Box::pin + Detach poll overhead.
  - pipeline.rs: BODY_RESP spans the single response_headers build, the RenderedBody
    Arc and page_response(status, HeaderMap, ..); L1 is recorded after the HIT branch
    whose page_response now takes (status, headers, len, ..). JOBS_CALL unchanged
    (Rec guard first in `if !misses.is_empty() {`).

